<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">António Coelho Guerreiro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1702">1702</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">António Coelho Guerreiro was a Portuguese administrator who arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lifau">Lifau</a> in 1702 as the first governor appointed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solor">Solor</a>. His arrival marked the start of formal Portuguese government on the island, though authority there remained long contested by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/topasses">Topasses</a>, the local Portuguese-speaking mestizo community.</p></div>
